<title>SWEDEN: Skanska wins $115 U.S. Fed contract.</title>
<headline>Skanska wins $115 U.S. Fed contract.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company Skanska said on Wednesday its U.S. unit Beers won a $115 million order for a building in Atlanta, Georgia for the Federal Reserve for a bank note printing plant.</p>
<p>Work will be completed in 2000, Skanska said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
